expected_issues.description:
Potential performance regression: `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT.write(...)` is now executed inline (no `executor.execute(...)`). If this write performs blocking IO to the blob store, it will directly occupy a SNAPSHOT thread and may reduce throughput / increase tail latency. Previously it was still scheduled on the same executor, but at least it yielded to the executor queue and avoided deep synchronous execution within the listener chain.

Suggestion: keep the `executor.execute(ActionRunnable.run(...))` pattern (or ensure `SNAPSHOT_FORMAT.write` is guaranteed fast/non-blocking) and document why it is safe to run inline.

```suggestion
                    executor.execute(
                        ActionRunnable.run(
                            allMetaListeners.acquire(),
                            () -> SNAPSHOT_FORMAT.write(snapshotInfo, blobContainer(), snapshotId.getUUID(), compress)
                        )
                    );
```

